mode: "100644"
text: "# The RANKS framework — lists & roundups that earn the slot\n\nA list ranks things, so the skill must rank *honestly* and make every entry earn its place. Each letter is a\ngate; weak lists fail at R (padded premise) or N (filler entries).\n\n## R — Right-size the premise\nA list people actually search/want, with a **number that serves the content, not a target to hit.** Don't pad to\n\"25\" and don't starve a great list at 5 — the count follows the genuinely-good items. Pick the type that fits:\n\"best X for [specific Y]\", \"N ways to [outcome]\", expert roundup, product/tool roundup, or a curated link\nroundup. The title states the payoff up front (number + promise + who it's for). One premise, one clear promise.\n\n## A — Assemble honestly\nCurate real, vetted items and **rank by genuine merit against stated criteria** (say how you judged). The\nnon-negotiables:\n- **No fabricated items, no fake quotes, no invented rankings.**\n- **Disclose** affiliate/sponsor/own-product (FTC); don't rank by commission; don't auto-#1 yourself — an\n  independent, criteria-based ranking is what compounds and gets cited.\n- For roundups: **real contributors, with consent**; the human does outreach, the agent drafts the ask.\n- Verify product facts (pricing/specs/claims) — the human checks; the agent doesn't guess.\n\n## N — Nail every entry\nEach item is a mini-payload that earns its slot: **the what + the why-it-matters + one specific detail** (a\nresult, a \"Best For\" tag, a real example). Cut filler — the **weakest entry sets the perceived quality** of the\nwhole list. Outcome-anchored beats generic (\"the tool we used to do X\", not \"a good tool\"). Name entities\nexplicitly (tools/brands/people) — it's what both readers and AI extract.\n\n## K — Keep the scroll moving\nOrder for impact: lead with the best or most-surprising item (or a deliberate arc that builds), front-load the\nhook (hands to `hook-writer`), and keep it **ruthlessly scannable** — the format's entire advantage is\nskimmability. Consistent structure per entry. A summary line or quick table aids both humans and AI extraction.\n\n## S — Spread + atomize\nOne list = many cuts, and roundups have built-in reach:\n- **Atomize:** whole list → carousel/thread; **1 item = 1 standalone post**; top 3 → short video.\n- **Roundups:** contributors amplify → route to `collabs-and-cross-promotion`.\n- **\"Best of\":** engineer for AI citation + place for search; refresh on a cadence (lists decay).\n- Route mechanics to the format writers; **WoopSocial publishes**; measure saves/shares + clicks — never a\n  fabricated metric or ranking.\n"
